OUTPUT SUMMARY
--------------

- The file "results_aggregated.dat" contains all measurements aggregated.
  Number in parenthesis next to the protein name, is the number of monomers.
  For each lysine entry, mean and standard deviation of pKa over all monomers is given.
  In parenthesis after pKa data, the number of lysines calculation was performed on.
  The number or lysine can be inferion to number of monomers either because some monomers may miss specific lysines, or calculations encountered problems.

- The file "top20.dat" contains the 20 lysines with lowest pKa.
  Only included lysines having at least two measurements from different proteins).

- The file "chains_summary.dat" lists, for each protein, the chain names in the atomic structure.
  Tab separation between protein name and list of chain IDs.
